  "extraction_contract": {
    "unit": "Select ab[@type=recipe] with no ancestor ab[@type=recipe]. Retain nested subrecipes once within their enclosing full unit; preserve their ranges as provenance, never emit them again as independent units. Non-recipe ab and collection-level headings are outside this recipe contract.",
    "ordered_text": "Traverse XML mixed content in document order; emit each text and tail once. Suppress note subtree content and all attributes. Retain inner text of semantic wrappers (ingredient, instruction, alternative, tool, etc.) and ref text. Never emit en, key, commodity, ana, IDs or target values.",
    "heading_body": "Retain title text in its original position and mark its character span. Titles occur inside opener/instruction/closer/servingTip and are not universally separate authorial rubrics. Never move all titles to a heading prefix, duplicate them, or silently drop them from full text. Empty title[type=none] has no authorial text; its English key is not a missing heading to fill.",
    "word_boundaries": "Preserve literal character order and whitespace; XML inline tag boundaries add no space. Whitespace-collapse only after concatenation, retaining a raw representation for audit. pb is layout-only, does not automatically introduce a lexical boundary. No case folding, transliteration, spelling correction, abbreviation expansion or punctuation stripping at intake. No w token elements occur; tokenization for fitting remains separately preregistered.",
    "missing_text": "Exclude whole top-level units from the complete-text subset if any descendant unclear/gap/supplied/choice occurs, literal bracketed lacuna appears, or an editorial note states truncation, missing text, mid-recipe start or contamination by another recipe. Keep reason and original source pointer. Completeness means no explicit flag in this edition, not proven complete authorial original. Semantic-identification uncertainty in a note alone does not remove otherwise readable text.",
    "choices_and_variants": "No choice/supplied/gap elements observed in these body XMLs. If encountered after an input update, fail closed for full-text eligibility; do not concatenate alternatives or guess preferred editorial readings. alternative elements HERE encode authorial cooking alternatives and must retain their entire text, not select a branch.",
    "diplomatic_limit": "These are semantic-annotation derivatives with manuscript spelling; absence of original facsimile/collation prevents certifying a strictly diplomatic transcription. Local headers themselves describe editorial transcription conventions."
  },
  "concrete_pitfalls": [
    "w1 and b4 editorial notes include English Recipe breaks off.; gr1 notes identify missing text, mid-recipe starts and continuation of another recipe.",
    "b6 uses literal […] and [...] inside text, including partial words, despite zero gap/unclear XML tags.",
    "bs1 has 1 unclear element and gr1 has 3 in recipe scope.",
    "Naive itertext includes modern bilingual annotation notes; naive space-joining all text nodes adds false lexical boundaries.",
    "Nested subrecipe elements create double counting when both descendant ab nodes and their full parents are emitted.",
    "gr1 editorial note says food lists fol. 87r–93v were not included: this XML is not a complete codex transcript."
  ],
